WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Polymers and composites. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Compare layered and single-material behavior

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A composite combines constituents to achieve a tailored structure. Direction matters because layered materials may respond differently along and across fibers.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Sketch load parallel and perpendicular to a fiber direction; do not use one isotropic number for both.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Use-case matching

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Material category alone does not guarantee strength, durability or safety.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Compare layered and single-material behavior
